[38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ Logout scope [39m[49m

[1m[38;5;231mShould the design include a minimal session indicator and logout control?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mInclude both (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mA 'Signed in as X' line rendered from getSession() on load, plus a logout button calling clearSession(). Makes the
[39m     [38;5;246mfeature verifiable and prevents a permanently stuck session.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Logout only
     [38;5;246mAdd the logout control so the session can be cleared, but no indicator. Fixes the stuck-session defect; the feature
[39m     [38;5;246mstays hard to verify by hand.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Neither — module only
     [38;5;246mShip src/session.js and the login wiring alone. clearSession() lands with no caller and the stored identity cannot
[39m     [38;5;246mbe cleared from the UI.[39m
